cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: DeterministicSequentialEmission.jl
abstract: >-
  The deterministic sequential emission treatment of prompt neutron emission from fission
  fragments: the energy conservation equation of every emission sequence is solved separately,
  with Weisskopf-Ewing evaporation spectra in the centre-of-mass system and fragment level
  densities in the Fermi-gas regime. Because the number of sequences n is an integer at every
  fragment configuration, every product mass A − 1 … A − n is an integer, so the post-neutron
  products are distributed without rounding: by default a chain ends on each of its n residuals
  with probability 1/n, so that the products lose the multiplicity, and the published count,
  A_p = A − n, is an option. Multiplicities, residual quantities, the laboratory prompt neutron
  spectrum, the post-neutron product yields and kinetic energies, and the excitation energy left
  for prompt γ rays are contracted against measured fragment yields.
type: software
authors:
